\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
We presented a Lyapunov-Inspired Future-Aware PPO agent for adaptive video streaming. By incorporating immediate future chunk sizes into the state space and utilizing a Lyapunov drift penalty, our agent learns a robust policy that successfully solves the fundamental plasticity-stability dilemma. Experimental results demonstrate that our method outperforms traditional control-theoretic algorithms (RobustMPC) and pure DRL baselines (Pensieve) in overall QoE, while crucially reducing chaotic bitrate oscillations by over 91\% compared to RobustMPC. Furthermore, zero-shot evaluations on extreme 5G mmWave networks prove our agent's real-world deployability. While traditional and learning-based baselines suffer catastrophic failures (yielding up to 129 seconds of stalling) during sudden signal blockages, our agent dynamically bounds rebuffering risks to acceptable limits, successfully maintaining the highest practical QoE. In future work, we plan to extend this hybrid framework to live video streaming scenarios where future chunk sizes must be dynamically forecasted, and explore the dynamic adaptation of the reference buffer threshold ($B_{ref}$) based on real-time network volatility.

